<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-1298] Data and Meta in IGFS should be updated in one transaction.</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-1298</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Tests written to check behavior &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-1277&quot; title=&quot;Enable cache backup functionality for IGFS&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-1277&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-1277&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; revealed problems on file data writing when some nodes have left the topology (see tests added in &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-1277&quot; title=&quot;Enable cache backup functionality for IGFS&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-1277&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-1277&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;). &lt;br/&gt;
In particular, meta data and file data are processed in separate transactions. So, one can complete while another may not. To fix that we need to link them together in one transaction.&lt;br/&gt;
In more detail, this means that blocks writing and appropriate file size update should happen in one transaction.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="12858693">IGNITE-1298</key>
            <summary>Data and Meta in IGFS should be updated in one transaction.</summary>
